    "blocks_jgTJWD": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_19f144a_kVmwE7": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_19f144a",
          "settings": {
            "line_1_text": "Timeless Grace",
            "line_1_alignment": "left",
            "line_1_offset": 300,
            "line_2_text": "vs",
            "line_2_alignment": "center",
            "line_2_offset": 0,
            "line_3_text": "Coco Mademoiselle by Chanel:",
            "line_3_alignment": "right",
            "line_3_offset": -40,
            "body_text": "<p>Coco Mademoiselle is the benchmark for a certain kind of feminine fragrance. Clean, grown-up, and immediately recognisable. It has been the top-selling women's perfume in the UK and US for years. The EDP retails at around $160 for 100ml and it earns that position consistently.</p><p><strong>Timeless Grace</strong> opens with the same fresh orange and bergamot, develops through jasmine and rose, and settles into a warm patchouli base that wears throughout the day. The comparison test here produced the closest result of the three: on dry-down, both fragrances sat in the same warm, clean territory. The original has a very slight additional depth in the base that reflects the higher concentration of raw materials, but it is a difference you would only notice if you were specifically looking for it.<br/><br/>At around $20 versus $160, Timeless Grace makes a compelling case for anyone who loves the Coco Mademoiselle profile but wants to wear it every day without the creeping sense that they should be saving it for something more significant.</p>",
            "line_1_size": 44,
            "line_2_size": 85,
            "line_3_size": 44,
            "body_size": 22,
            "line_2_margin_top": 30,
            "line_3_margin_top": 4,
            "header_spacing": 40,
            "body_max_width": 1000,
            "section_padding_top": 60,
            "section_padding_bottom": 60,
            "background_color": "#ffffff",
            "text_color": "#121212"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_19f144a_kVmwE7"
      ],
      "disabled": true,
      "name": "Staggered typography",
      "settings": {}
    },
    "17786893180b60ea14": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_c88e324_m8PFU4": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_c88e324",
          "settings": {
            "container_width": 1200,
            "left_column_width": 40,
            "right_column_width": 60,
            "column_gap": 40,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "heading": "Where The Differences actually Show Up",
            "heading_font": "serif",
            "heading_size": 56,
            "mobile_heading_size": 40,
            "heading_color": "#000000",
            "heading_indent": 10,
            "mobile_heading_indent": 40,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/magnific_luxury-perfume-comparison_74h5S6MJAL_jpg.jpg",
            "image_max_width": 600,
            "heading_image_gap": 4,
            "mobile_heading_image_gap": 25,
            "body_text": "<p>Across all our tests, the differences between inspired fragrances and originals came down to three things.<br/><br/><strong>Concentration of raw materials</strong>. Designer houses use extremely high concentrations of expensive ingredients. The originals have a certain richness in the base that reflects this. A well-made inspired fragrance gets close, but the very finest nuances of a $300 bottle are sometimes in those base notes, and it is worth knowing that going in.<br/><br/><strong>Projection in the opening</strong>. Top notes on the originals tend to radiate a little further, particularly in the first half an hour after applying. This matters if you are spraying in an elevator and want to make an immediate impression. It matters less if you are wearing something all day for yourself.<br/><br/><strong>Longevity on dry skin</strong>. Both perform significantly better on moisturised skin. On dry skin, the originals do have a slight edge in staying power. The fix is twelve seconds of moisturiser before you spray. After that, the gap closes considerably.</p>",
            "body_font": "system_ui_n4",
            "body_size": 24,
            "mobile_body_size": 16,
            "body_color": "#000000",
            "paragraph_spacing": 30,
            "mobile_paragraph_spacing": 15,
            "text_vertical_offset": 10,
            "background_color": "#ffffff",
            "padding_top": 100,
            "padding_bottom": 100,
            "horizontal_padding": 40,
            "mobile_padding_top": 60,
            "mobile_padding_bottom": 60,
            "mobile_horizontal_padding": 20,
            "mobile_gap": 30
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_c88e324_m8PFU4"
      ],
      "disabled": true,
      "settings": {}
    },
    "blocks_NgyNz4": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_qVFqqX": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_fb81b45",
          "settings": {
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "max_width": 1200,
            "section_padding": 20,
            "background_color": "#f9f6f1",
            "heading": "<p>The one that shows up confident: Invictor (inspired by Aventus by Creed)</p>",
            "heading_size": 60,
            "heading_color": "#000000",
            "heading_spacing": 10,
            "box_color": "#8b1d22",
            "box_radius": 25,
            "box_padding": 40,
            "box_spacing": 10,
            "box_paragraph_1": "<p>Aventus built its reputation as the fragrance for men who have figured things out. Invictor brings that same pineapple and birch opening into a smoky, mossy dry-down that is confident and clean at once. A best cologne for men that projects well without taking over, which is a harder balance to land than most people realize.</p><p><br/>Wear it on the kind of date where you want to show up as the best version of<br/>yourself. It will handle its end of that deal.</p>",
            "box_paragraph_2": "",
            "box_paragraph_3": "",
            "box_text_color": "#ffffff",
            "box_text_size": 22,
            "box_text_line_height": 1.6,
            "paragraph_spacing": 25,
            "subheading": "<p>The one that never misses: Marine (inspired by Bleu de Chanel)</p>",
            "subheading_size": 60,
            "subheading_color": "#000000",
            "subheading_spacing": 40,
            "bottom_text": "<p>Bleu de Chanel earned its place as a staple because it delivers every single time.<br/>Marine takes that same blueprint, clean citrus, warm ginger, dry sandalwood, and<br/>brings it to a price that makes reaching for it a simple call. A men's fragrance that<br/>reads as pulled-together and easy at once. No overthinking required. Save that<br/>energy for the conversation.</p>",
            "bottom_text_size": 22,
            "bottom_text_color": "#000000",
            "bottom_text_line_height": 1.6
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_qVFqqX"
      ],
      "settings": {}
    },
    "blocks_JXTkRM": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_KfenDP": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_fb81b45",
          "settings": {
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "max_width": 1200,
            "section_padding": 20,
            "background_color": "#f9f6f1",
            "heading": "",
            "heading_size": 56,
            "heading_color": "#000000",
            "heading_spacing": 10,
            "box_color": "#8b1d22",
            "box_radius": 25,
            "box_padding": 40,
            "box_spacing": 10,
            "box_paragraph_1": "",
            "box_paragraph_2": "",
            "box_paragraph_3": "",
            "box_text_color": "#ffffff",
            "box_text_size": 22,
            "box_text_line_height": 1.6,
            "paragraph_spacing": 25,
            "subheading": "<p>The one that gets a comment before the appetizers arrive: Fierce (inspired by Sauvage Parfum by Dior)</p>",
            "subheading_size": 56,
            "subheading_color": "#000000",
            "subheading_spacing": 40,
            "bottom_text": "<p>Sauvage is one of the most recognized men's fragrances in the world, and the reason is not complicated: it works every time. Fierce takes that ambroxan and pepper combination over a rich woody base and brings real presence to it. The kind of scent that tends to get a \"what are you wearing?\" before the night is an hour old.</p><p><br/>Use it with a little restraint. It is already doing the heavy lifting.</p>",
            "bottom_text_size": 22,
            "bottom_text_color": "#000000",
            "bottom_text_line_height": 1.6
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
